[#:seon.task{:name "run-answers-a-whole-namespace-without-a-verdict"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(`my.test/run`) in seon.render.value-test ran all 52 members to test one new deftest: over 30 s, past MCP's default bound, which answered only a timeout with no handle (the run finished and recorded at 22:04:14). Its answer is a vector of 52 per-test maps in symbol order, so the shown text starts with green members and the one red test is cut. Answer passed?, counts and the red members first (`seon.test/tally`'s verdict) and accept a named test or the tests naming a task, as `my.test/check` does for changes."
             :must-read #{my.test/run-owned seon.test/tally}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/repl-dogfood-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "run-owned-reply-repeats-its-output"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`my.test/run-owned` answers about 800 tokens for one test, with a duplicated :out. Done when the reply is focused through the render (one output, the verdict, the failing assertions' data) and its token size is asserted in a regression."
             :must-read #{my.test/run-owned}
             :evidence #{"tmp/repl-audit/change.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "check-in-the-defining-pass-says-the-test-does-not-exist"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(deftest inc3-fails ...) (`my.test/check` {`:seon.test/changed` ['scratch.msgs/inc3-fails]}) in one pass answers \"Changed identity has no definition, history or incoming edge.\" with :expected :complete-comparable-program-evidence (default 2026-10-08); the deftest's facts settle with the pass, and the same call next pass runs it. The defn and deftest record at settlement, so the check cannot see them; this breaks the confirmed ruling that a same-pass check sees the new definition (also hit by lane impl-hook, RF-4 at 3c15a3434). Done per ledger row MS-11b: a same-pass check reads the live world for the names the pass defined and runs the test, with no refusal."
             :must-read #{my.test/check}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/agent-messages/messages-opus-messages.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-check-no-test-reaches-reads-as-a-failure"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(`my.test/check` {`:seon.test/changed` [sym]}) for a symbol that no test reaches answers :passed? false with empty :results (lane impl-hook, RF-4 at 3c15a3434), which reads as a failure. Correct: the answer says as data that no test reaches the symbol, distinct from a red run. Proof: a my.test-test deftest (to be written) checking an unreached symbol asserts that datum and no :passed? false."
             :must-read #{my.test/check}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/schedule/cards/RF-4.md"}}]
